---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CO2BraytonCycle from '../components/CO2BraytonCycle.svelte';
import UnderConstructionOverlay from '../components/UnderConstructionOverlay.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="CO2 Brayton">
  <UnderConstructionOverlay />
  <section class="co2-hero">
    <div class="co2-align">
      <div class="title-row">
        <svg class="molecule" aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 48 30"><defs><pattern id="mol-knob-tex" patternUnits="objectBoundingBox" patternContentUnits="objectBoundingBox" width="1" height="1"><image href="/buttons/knob-silver.png" x="0" y="0" width="1" height="1" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid slice"/></pattern></defs><line class="mol-bond" x1="24" y1="13.4" x2="8" y2="13.4"/><line class="mol-bond" x1="24" y1="16.6" x2="8" y2="16.6"/><line class="mol-bond" x1="24" y1="13.4" x2="40" y2="13.4"/><line class="mol-bond" x1="24" y1="16.6" x2="40" y2="16.6"/><circle class="mol-o" cx="8" cy="15" r="6"/><circle class="mol-c" cx="24" cy="15" r="6.5"/><circle class="mol-o" cx="40" cy="15" r="6"/><circle class="mol-o-tint" cx="8" cy="15" r="6"/><circle class="mol-c-tint" cx="24" cy="15" r="6.5"/><circle class="mol-o-tint" cx="40" cy="15" r="6"/><text class="mol-label mol-label-o" x="8" y="15">O</text><text class="mol-label mol-label-c" x="24" y="15">C</text><text class="mol-label mol-label-o" x="40" y="15">O</text></svg>
        <h2 class="page-title">Supercritical CO<sub>2</sub> Recompression Brayton Cycle</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="scroll-hint">
        <span>Scroll for simulator</span>
        <svg class="scroll-hint-arrow" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" aria-hidden="true">
          <polyline points="3,6 8,11 13,6" />
        </svg>
      </div>
      <div class="cycle-intro">
        <p>
          The Brayton cycle you might already know from gas turbines runs on ordinary
          air: compress it, add heat, expand it through a turbine, dump the exhaust.
          Swap the air for carbon dioxide and keep the whole loop above CO<sub>2</sub>'s
          critical point (7.38 MPa, 31 °C) instead of venting to atmosphere, and you get
          a closed-loop supercritical CO<sub>2</sub> (sCO<sub>2</sub>) Brayton cycle. Above
          the critical point, CO<sub>2</sub> never boils, it just gets progressively denser
          as pressure rises, so the compressor inlet sits in a liquid-like, high-density
          region where compression work is far lower than compressing a normal gas. That
          single fact is what makes sCO<sub>2</sub> cycles compact: smaller compressors,
          smaller turbines, a fraction of the footprint of an equivalent steam plant, which
          is a big part of why they keep coming up in Gen IV fission, concentrated solar,
          and now fusion balance-of-plant studies.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Recompression</strong> is the fix for a problem specific to this fluid.
          A plain regenerative Brayton cycle, one recuperator recovering heat from the
          turbine exhaust to preheat the compressor discharge, runs into trouble near
          CO<sub>2</sub>'s critical point. Specific heat spikes there, and it spikes
          asymmetrically: the cold, dense stream heading into the heater has a much higher
          cp than the hot, lower-density stream coming off the turbine. A single recuperator
          sized to avoid a temperature crossover at one end ends up oversized, and full of
          irreversibility, everywhere else. The standard fix, modeled here, splits the
          stream after a low-temperature recuperator: part of it goes straight to a second,
          auxiliary compressor without being cooled first, and only the rest passes through
          the precooler to the main compressor. That keeps both recuperators' hot and cold
          streams closer in heat capacity across their whole length, which is what actually
          fixes the pinch.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Layout</strong> follows that recompression architecture: a turbine expanding
          from the intermediate loop's peak temperature, a reheat pass partway through the
          expansion to pick up more heat before the low-pressure stage, then a high-temperature
          recuperator (HTR) and low-temperature recuperator (LTR) in series recovering as much
          of that exhaust heat as their effectiveness allows, a main compressor and a
          recompressor splitting the return flow as described above, and a precooler ahead of
          the main compressor rejecting the rest to the circulating-water/cooling-tower loop.
        </p>
        <p>
          Both the turbine inlet and the reheat inlet draw straight from the same solar-salt
          intermediate loop as the Rankine cycle, 565 °C supply from the Secondary HTX, so the
          sliders here are capped at 560 °C: push either one to a full round 600 °C and you'd
          be asking the CO<sub>2</sub> to leave the heat exchanger hotter than the salt
          supplying it, which no heat exchanger can do.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="hero-bottom-bar"></div>
  <div class="co2-align diagram-title-row">
    <h3 class="page-title">Supercritical CO<sub>2</sub> Recompression Brayton Cycle Diagram</h3>
  </div>
  <div class="page-breakout">
    <img class="cycle-diagram diagram-co2" src="/diagrams/fusion-co2-brayton.png" alt="Process flow diagram of the supercritical CO2 recompression Brayton cycle balance of plant" width="1653" height="800" />
  </div>
  <p class="co2-align diagram-credit">
    Cycle layout adapted from
    Colliva, F.; Ciurluini, C.; Iaboni, A.; Centomani, G.V.; Trotta, A.; Giannetti, F.
    "Analysis of Power Conversion System Options for ARC-like Tokamak Fusion Reactor
    Balance of Plant." <em>Sustainability</em> <strong>2024</strong>, <em>16</em>, 7480. <a href="https://doi.org/10.3390/su16177480" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">doi.org/10.3390/su16177480</a>
  </p>
  <div class="simulator-box chamfer-panel chamfer-all">
    <!-- plain div, not CO2BraytonCycle directly. astro's own astro-island wrapper
         is display:contents, so chamfer-panel's z-index promotion no-ops on it. -->
    <div><CO2BraytonCycle client:load /></div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* sized off this diagram's native resolution, same scale factor as rankine and he diagrams for consistent label size */
  .diagram-co2 { max-width: 1050px; }

  .co2-align {
    max-width: 1028px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* full-bleed teal-fade hero, same recipe as the rankine page */
  .co2-hero {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    margin: -24px -24px 0;
    padding: 40px max(24px, calc(50vw - 640px)) 32px;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(53, 214, 180, 0.11), rgba(53, 214, 180, 0) 88%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.22), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0) 42%),
      linear-gradient(163deg, var(--steel-300), var(--steel-500) 85%);
    background-blend-mode: normal;
    background-size: cover;
    background-position: center;
  }

  /* decorative CO2 molecule flanking the title, three knob-textured atoms with a
     double-bond pair of lines on each side, same construction as the rankine
     page's H2O molecule. title-row is a positioning anchor: the molecule is
     absolutely positioned into the left margin so it never shifts the title
     text, which stays flush with the same left edge as the rest of the page. */
  .title-row {
    position: relative;
  }
  .title-row .page-title {
    font-size: 30px;
  }
  .molecule {
    position: absolute;
    right: 100%;
    top: 50%;
    transform: translateY(-50%);
    margin-right: 14px;
    width: 128px;
    height: auto;
    opacity: 0.95;
  }
  @media (max-width: 1220px) {
    .molecule { display: none; }
  }
  .molecule .mol-bond { stroke: var(--steel-900); stroke-width: 1.6; stroke-linecap: round; }
  .molecule .mol-o { fill: url(#mol-knob-tex); }
  .molecule .mol-c { fill: url(#mol-knob-tex); }
  /* same teal wash the slider thumbs lay over their knob texture, so the atoms read as the site's metal, not raw chrome */
  .molecule .mol-o-tint { fill: var(--teal); opacity: 0.5; pointer-events: none; }
  .molecule .mol-c-tint { fill: var(--teal-dim); opacity: 0.6; pointer-events: none; }
  .molecule .mol-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-weight: 700;
    fill: #ffffff;
    text-anchor: middle;
    dominant-baseline: central;
  }
  .molecule .mol-label-o { font-size: 6.5px; }
  .molecule .mol-label-c { font-size: 7px; }

  .scroll-hint {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 6px;
    margin: 2px 0 18px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--teal-dim);
  }
  .scroll-hint-arrow {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--teal-dim);
    stroke-width: 2;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .cycle-intro {
    margin-top: 4px;
  }
  .cycle-intro p {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-weight: 500;
    margin: 0 0 12px;
  }
  .cycle-intro p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .cycle-intro strong { color: var(--paper); font-weight: 700; }

  /* brushed-metal strip matching the nav bar's chamfer-panel rim weight */
  .hero-bottom-bar {
    position: relative;
    isolation: isolate;
    height: 16px;
    margin: 0 -24px;
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35), transparent 40%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, var(--steel-650), var(--steel-800));
    background-repeat: no-repeat, no-repeat;
    background-size: 100% 100%, 100% 100%;
    background-position: center, center;
    border-top: 1.5px solid var(--steel-900);
    border-bottom: 1.5px solid var(--steel-900);
    box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12), inset 0 1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5), inset 0 -1px 0 rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.5);
  }
  /* aluminum grain: two copies of the same fixed-width tile, offset by half
     a tile and cross-faded between - see BaseLayout.astro's .site-nav. */
  .hero-bottom-bar::before,
  .hero-bottom-bar::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background-image: var(--aluminum);
    background-repeat: repeat-x;
    background-size: 900px auto;
    background-position: 0 center;
    mix-blend-mode: overlay;
    pointer-events: none;
    -webkit-mask-image: repeating-linear-gradient(to right, transparent 0%, black 15%, black 85%, transparent 100%);
    mask-image: repeating-linear-gradient(to right, transparent 0%, black 15%, black 85%, transparent 100%);
    -webkit-mask-size: 900px 100%;
    mask-size: 900px 100%;
    -webkit-mask-repeat: repeat-x;
    mask-repeat: repeat-x;
    -webkit-mask-position: 0 center;
    mask-position: 0 center;
  }
  .hero-bottom-bar::after {
    background-position: 450px center;
    -webkit-mask-position: 450px center;
    mask-position: 450px center;
  }

  /* spacing so the title isn't flush against the bar above */
  .diagram-title-row {
    margin-top: 32px;
  }

  .diagram-credit {
    margin: 4px auto 28px;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-dim);
    font-weight: 500;
  }
  .diagram-credit em { font-style: italic; }
  .diagram-credit a {
    color: var(--teal-dim);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .diagram-credit a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
